From: Alfre <alfredopennisi3@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 23:44:37 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] DXF/DWG reading: textbox hatch loops and table text height

- A textbox boundary (group 92 bit 8) frames text inside a hatch: a hole so
  the fill stays off the text. Files also flag it external (92 = 9) and with
  the outer style it was filled as a solid box over the text (title block
  fields). Textbox loops are left out.
- A table from another writer takes its text height from its style; a DWG
  converted to DXF can lose the cells' own height (no 140 in the cells),
  while the anonymous *T block that draws the table still shows it. The
  most common text height in that block now sets the table's height.
